            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>An apparatus, system, and method for additive manufacturing are disclosed. The method includes controlling a first print head (202) to print an outer contour (102) for a layer of a part and controlling a second print head (204) to print an infrared-actuated print material (206) within the outer contour (102). An infrared actuator (210) is then controlled to cause the infrared-actuated print material (206) to flow within the contour (102), thereby filling gaps (106, 110) and improving the structural integrity of the part. The apparatus may be configured without a dispenser for an anti-heat agent, as the physically printed outer contour (102) renders such an agent unnecessary, thereby simplifying the manufacturing process.</p>
            </abstract>
